# ==============================================================================
# Query Name: 06_high_volume_bruteforce_detection.spl
# Project: P1 — Splunk SOC Home Lab & Log Analysis
# Purpose: High-volume brute-force detection alert rule
# Security Use Case: Operational SIEM alert trigger logic for automated ticketing and response
# ==============================================================================

index=main (event_type="Failed SSH Login" OR event_type="Multiple Failed Authentication Attempts")
| stats count by id.orig_h
| where count >= 5

# Expected Interpretation:
# - Real-time or scheduled saved search query evaluating inbound authentication attempts.
# - Fires an alert when any single source IP exceeds 5 failed attempts in the time window.
# - Triggers email notification to SOC tier-1 queue and executes dynamic blocklist updates.
